## 🚀 Setup & Installation

### Prerequisites

- **Python** 3.10 or higher
- **Node.js** 18 or higher
- **Git**
- **Google Gemini API Key** → [Get it free here](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/guardian-risk-intelligence.git
cd guardian-risk-intelligence
2️⃣ Backend Setup
bash
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Activate (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Create .env file
copy .env.example .env      # Windows
cp .env.example .env        # Mac/Linux
# Now edit .env and add your GEMINI_API_KEY

# Initialize DB & seed data
python -m app.utils.seed_data

# Train ML model (one-time)
python -m app.ml.train_model

# Run backend
uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
Backend will run at → http://localhost:8000
API docs → http://localhost:8000/docs

3️⃣ Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Create .env
copy .env.example .env      # Windows
cp .env.example .env        # Mac/Linux

# Run dev server
npm run dev
Frontend will run at → http://localhost:5173

🔐 Environment Variables
Backend .env
env
# App
APP_NAME=Guardian Risk Intelligence
APP_ENV=development
DEBUG=True

# Database
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./risk_intelligence.db

# Security
SECRET_KEY=your-super-secret-jwt-key-change-me
ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60

# Gemini AI
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-flash

# Streaming
STREAM_INTERVAL_SECONDS=3
Frontend .env
env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000/ws/stream
⚠️ Never commit real .env files. Only .env.example should be in Git.

🔌 API Endpoints
Authentication
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/auth/register	Register new user
POST	/api/auth/login	Login & get JWT
GET	/api/auth/me	Get current user
Risks
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/risks	List all risks (paginated)
GET	/api/risks/{id}	Get risk details
POST	/api/risks	Create risk manually
GET	/api/risks/stats	Aggregate stats
Mitigations
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/mitigations	List all mitigations
GET	/api/mitigations/{risk_id}	Mitigations for a risk
POST	/api/mitigations/generate/{risk_id}	Trigger Gemini generation
Graph
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/graph/full	Full risk graph (nodes + edges)
GET	/api/graph/centrality	Top central risks
GET	/api/graph/communities	Detected clusters
Analytics
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/analytics/trend	Risk trend over time
GET	/api/analytics/distribution	Category distribution
GET	/api/analytics/severity	Severity breakdown
Alerts
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/alerts	List alerts
POST	/api/alerts/{id}/ack	Acknowledge alert
WebSocket
Protocol	Endpoint	Description
WS	/ws/stream	Live risk event stream
🧠 Machine Learning Model
Model: RandomForestClassifier (scikit-learn)

Input Features:

risk_type (encoded)

source (encoded)

hour_of_day

day_of_week

historical_frequency

keywords_severity_score

Output:

severity_class: Low / Medium / High / Critical

risk_score: 0–100 (via regression model)

Training:

bash
python -m app.ml.train_model
Generates:

backend/app/ml/risk_classifier.pkl

backend/app/ml/scaler.pkl

Accuracy Target: ~85% on synthetic dataset (CPU-friendly).

🕸️ Graph Analytics
Built with NetworkX:

Nodes = Risk events

Edges = Shared attributes (same type, same source, within time window)

Metrics Computed:

Degree Centrality → Most connected risks

Betweenness Centrality → Bridge risks (critical)

Community Detection (Louvain) → Risk clusters

Cascading Paths → Chain reactions

Visualized on frontend using react-force-graph-2d with:

Node color = risk type

Node size = severity

Edge thickness = relationship strength

🤖 Gemini AI Integration
Model: gemini-1.5-flash

Prompt Strategy:

text
You are an enterprise risk mitigation expert.

Risk Details:
- Type: {risk_type}
- Title: {title}
- Description: {description}
- Severity: {severity}
- Risk Score: {score}

Generate a mitigation strategy in JSON with:
{
  "priority": "Low|Medium|High|Critical",
  "strategy": "Detailed action plan",
  "steps": ["step1", "step2", ...],
  "estimated_cost": "$X,XXX",
  "timeline": "X days",
  "owner_department": "e.g., IT, Legal, Finance"
}
Response parsed and stored in the mitigations table.

