🚨 PART 6: Common Errors & Solutions
❌ Error 1: mkdir : Cannot create a file when that file already exists
Solution: -Force flag use kar:

powershell
mkdir folder_name -Force
❌ Error 2: New-Item : The file already exists
Solution: -Force add kar:

powershell
New-Item filename -ItemType File -Force
❌ Error 3: fatal: not a git repository
Solution: Check kar ki sahi folder mein hai:

powershell
git status
# Agar fail ho, toh:
git init
❌ Error 4: PowerShell mkdir a, b, c kaam nahi kar raha
Solution: Comma-separated list PowerShell mein supported hai, but agar error aaye toh ek-ek karke chala:

powershell
mkdir backend
mkdir frontend
mkdir database
❌ Error 5: git add . mein .env bhi add ho rahi hai
Solution: .gitignore mein .env add hai kya check kar. Agar nahi toh force remove:

powershell
git rm --cached .env
git commit -m "Remove .env from tracking"
✅ PART 7: Final Verification Checklist
Yeh sab verify kar push se pehle:

□ .gitignore file created with correct content
□ backend/ folder with all subfolders
□ frontend/ folder with all subfolders
□ database/ folder with schema.sql
□ docs/ folder with docs
□ scripts/, notebooks/, .github/ folders
□ .gitkeep files in empty folders
□ .env.example created (not .env)
□ README.md updated with detailed content
□ git status shows all files
□ .env file is NOT in git status output
🎯 Quick Copy-Paste Order
.gitignore file banao → upar wala content paste kar

One-shot mega command chala (Part 3)

tree /F chala ke verify kar

Git push commands chala (Part 4)

GitHub pe check kar (Part 5)

💡 Pro Tip
Agar tujhe folders sirf dekhne hain toh:

powershell
tree /F
Agar folder structure ko file mein save karna hai:

powershell
tree /F > structure.txt
Bhai, bas itna kar — .gitignore file banao, one-shot command chala, phir git push kar de. 2 minute ka kaam hai.

