⚡ PART 3: One-Shot Mega Command (Ek Saath Sab Kuch)
Agar tujhe sab ek saath karna hai bina baar-baar chale, toh yeh ek block copy-paste kar PowerShall mein:

powershell
# ---------- CREATE FOLDERS ----------
mkdir backend, backend\app, backend\app\models, backend\app\schemas, backend\app\routes, backend\app\services, backend\app\ml, backend\app\ml\datasets, backend\app\graph, backend\app\ai, backend\app\core, backend\app\websocket, backend\app\utils, backend\app\static, backend\tests, backend\migrations, backend\migrations\versions -Force

mkdir frontend, frontend\src, frontend\src\components, frontend\src\components\layout, frontend\src\components\ui, frontend\src\components\charts, frontend\src\components\risk, frontend\src\components\graph, frontend\src\components\mitigation, frontend\src\components\alerts, frontend\src\components\common, frontend\src\pages, frontend\src\hooks, frontend\src\services, frontend\src\context, frontend\src\store, frontend\src\utils, frontend\src\styles, frontend\src\routes, frontend\src\assets, frontend\src\assets\icons, frontend\src\assets\images, frontend\src\assets\fonts, frontend\public -Force

mkdir database, database\migrations, docs, docs\screenshots, docs\diagrams, scripts, notebooks, .github, .github\workflows -Force

# ---------- CREATE ROOT FILES ----------
New-Item .gitignore, .env.example, LICENSE, backend\requirements.txt, backend\.env.example, backend\Dockerfile, database\schema.sql, database\seed.sql, docs\architecture.md, docs\api_reference.md, docs\setup_guide.md -ItemType File -Force

# ---------- CREATE .gitkeep FILES ----------
Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Directory | ForEach-Object {
    $gitkeep = Join-Path $_.FullName ".gitkeep"
    if (-not (Get-ChildItem $_.FullName -File)) {
        New-Item $gitkeep -ItemType File -Force | Out-Null
    }
}

# ---------- SHOW STRUCTURE ----------
tree /F
Yeh 4 blocks — folders, root files, .gitkeep files sab bana dega. Aur last mein tree /F command se pura structure dikha dega.

📤 PART 4: Git Push Commands (GitHub Pe Upload)
Ek baar sab files ban jayein, phir yeh chala:

powershell
# 1. Status check
git status

# 2. Sab files add kar
git add .

# 3. Commit kar
git commit -m "Add complete project folder structure with .gitignore"

# 4. GitHub pe push kar
git push origin main
🔍 PART 5: Verify Kar — Kya Upload Hua
GitHub pe jaa → refresh kar → tujhe dikhega:

✅ .gitignore

✅ README.md

✅ LICENSE

✅ backend/ (all subfolders)

✅ frontend/ (all subfolders)

✅ database/

✅ docs/

✅ scripts/

✅ notebooks/

✅ .github/

Dhyan de: .env file GitHub pe nahi dikhni chahiye — kyunki .gitignore mein ignore kar di. Sirf .env.example dikhegi.

🚨 PART 6: Common Errors & Solutions
❌ Error 1: mkdir : Cannot create a file when that file already exists
Solution: -Force flag use kar:

powershell
mkdir folder_name -Force
❌ Error 2: New-Item : The file already exists
Solution: -Force add kar:

powershell
New-Item filename -ItemType File -Force
❌ Error 3: fatal: not a git repository
Solution: Check kar ki sahi folder mein hai:

powershell
git status
# Agar fail ho, toh:
git init
❌ Error 4: PowerShell mkdir a, b, c kaam nahi kar raha
Solution: Comma-separated list PowerShell mein supported hai, but agar error aaye toh ek-ek karke chala:

powershell
mkdir backend
mkdir frontend
mkdir database
❌ Error 5: git add . mein .env bhi add ho rahi hai
Solution: .gitignore mein .env add hai kya check kar. Agar nahi toh force remove:

powershell
git rm --cached .env
git commit -m "Remove .env from tracking"
✅ PART 7: Final Verification Checklist
Yeh sab verify kar push se pehle:

□ .gitignore file created with correct content
□ backend/ folder with all subfolders
□ frontend/ folder with all subfolders
□ database/ folder with schema.sql
□ docs/ folder with docs
□ scripts/, notebooks/, .github/ folders
□ .gitkeep files in empty folders
□ .env.example created (not .env)
□ README.md updated with detailed content
□ git status shows all files
□ .env file is NOT in git status output
🎯 Quick Copy-Paste Order
.gitignore file banao → upar wala content paste kar

One-shot mega command chala (Part 3)

tree /F chala ke verify kar

Git push commands chala (Part 4)

GitHub pe check kar (Part 5)

